---
import ContentPageHero from './ContentPageHero.astro';

const capabilities = [
    {
        label: 'Durable state',
        what: 'Your AI holds context across sessions, across days, across months. Nothing dissolves into chat history. What it learns, it keeps.',
    },
    {
        label: 'Background execution',
        what: 'Work runs while you sleep. Async jobs, scheduled tasks, bounded agents -- they execute, write state, and wait for your review.',
    },
    {
        label: 'Review surfaces',
        what: 'Nothing ships without your eyes on it. A dedicated interface for reviewing what your AI did, approving what matters, and catching what does not.',
    },
    {
        label: 'Search and retrieval',
        what: 'Everything you feed the system becomes retrievable. Your docs, your notes, your history -- indexed and queryable, not buried in scrollback.',
    },
    {
        label: 'Model agnostic',
        what: 'Use frontier models when you need the best reasoning. Run local when nothing should leave the building. Switch providers without losing a thing.',
    },
    {
        label: 'Secure by architecture',
        what: 'Privacy is not a policy toggle. Your data lives on your infrastructure, governed by your rules. There is no hosted backend you cannot inspect.',
    },
];

const objectives = [
    'Build an AI system around one person\'s actual needs -- not the average of a million users.',
    'Use AI at depth without giving up ownership of your data, your context, or your infrastructure.',
    'Start from a working system that you fork and make entirely your own.',
    'Do serious, professional-grade work in a way that still feels playful and deeply satisfying.',
];
---

<div class="grid gap-10 md:gap-12">
    <ContentPageHero eyebrow="GalexC">
        <Fragment slot="title">Your AI. For real this time.</Fragment>
    </ContentPageHero>

    <!-- Opening: validate, don't explain -->
    <section class="max-w-[46rem]">
        <div class="grid gap-5 text-lg leading-[1.8] text-[#4f4438]">
            <p class="m-0">
                You have already tried the tools. Some of them are genuinely
                good. But you have noticed that no single tool -- no matter
                how capable -- adds up to a system that deeply knows your
                work, holds your context over time, and compounds for you the
                way a professional environment should.
            </p>
            <p class="m-0">
                GalexC exists because we noticed the same thing. It is a
                complete, working AI environment built for technical
                professionals who expect their tools to go as deep as their
                work demands.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Objectives: the meat, immediately -->
    <section
        class="grid gap-5 border-t border-t-[rgba(120,113,108,0.14)] pt-6"
    >
        <div class="grid gap-2.5 max-w-[44rem]">
            <p class="eyebrow">Objectives</p>
            <h2
                class="m-0 font-[Cormorant_Garamond,serif] text-[clamp(1.9rem,3vw,2.55rem)] leading-[0.98] text-[#2b241d]"
            >
                What GalexC is trying to be.
            </h2>
        </div>
        <ol class="m-0 grid list-none gap-3 p-0 sm:grid-cols-2">
            {
                objectives.map((objective, index) => (
                    <li class="group relative grid gap-3 rounded-2xl border border-stone-400/14 bg-white/40 p-5 shadow-[inset_0_1px_0_rgba(255,255,255,0.55)] transition-[transform,border-color,box-shadow] duration-300 ease-[cubic-bezier(0.22,1,0.36,1)] hover:-translate-y-px hover:border-[rgba(21,74,122,0.2)] hover:shadow-[0_14px_30px_rgba(43,36,29,0.06),inset_0_1px_0_rgba(255,255,255,0.6)]">
                        <header class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-2">
                            <span class="font-['IBM_Plex_Mono',monospace] text-[0.68rem] tracking-[0.18em] text-[#7a6d60] uppercase">
                                {String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}
                            </span>
                            <span
                                aria-hidden="true"
                                class="block h-px w-10 bg-[rgba(120,113,108,0.22)] transition-colors duration-300 group-hover:bg-[rgba(21,74,122,0.32)]"
                            />
                        </header>
                        <p class="m-0 leading-relaxed text-[#4f4438]">
                            {objective}
                        </p>
                    </li>
                ))
            }
        </ol>

        <aside
            class="grid max-w-[46rem] gap-2 border-l-2 border-l-[rgba(21,74,122,0.18)] pl-5"
        >
            <p
                class="m-0 font-['IBM_Plex_Mono',monospace] text-[0.6rem] tracking-[0.18em] text-[#154a7a] uppercase"
            >
                Why bother
            </p>
            <p class="m-0 text-base leading-[1.8] text-[#564a3f]">
                If GalexC achieves its objectives, it could make room for better
                work, better decisions, and a better way of moving through the
                digital world. If it never becomes more than what it is today, a
                personal project that has been genuinely, deeply fun to build, I
                count this as a success.
            </p>
        </aside>
    </section>

    <!-- The one-liner: punctuation after objectives -->
    <section>
        <figure
            class="relative grid justify-items-center gap-5 overflow-hidden rounded-[1.35rem_0.95rem_1.15rem_0.92rem] border border-stone-400/14 bg-[linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(255,255,255,0.5),rgba(251,247,241,0.52)),repeating-linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(120,113,108,0.038)_0,rgba(120,113,108,0.038)_1px,transparent_1px,transparent_33px)] px-6 py-10 text-center shadow-[0_10px_28px_rgba(43,36,29,0.04),inset_0_1px_0_rgba(255,255,255,0.62)] md:px-10 md:py-14"
        >
            <span
                aria-hidden="true"
                class="pointer-events-none absolute -top-12 -right-12 h-44 w-44 rounded-full bg-[radial-gradient(circle,rgba(21,74,122,0.1),transparent_72%)]"
            ></span>
            <span
                aria-hidden="true"
                class="pointer-events-none absolute -bottom-16 -left-12 h-48 w-48 rounded-full bg-[radial-gradient(circle,rgba(180,83,9,0.08),transparent_70%)]"
            ></span>

            <p
                class="m-0 font-['IBM_Plex_Mono',monospace] text-[0.6rem] tracking-[0.22em] text-[#154a7a] uppercase"
            >
                In one line
            </p>

            <blockquote class="m-0 w-full">
                <p
                    class="m-0 text-[clamp(2.2rem,3.8vw,3rem)] leading-none text-[#2b241d] [text-wrap:balance]"
                    style="font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', serif;"
                >
                    Professional-grade personal AI.
                </p>
            </blockquote>

            <span
                aria-hidden="true"
                class="block h-px w-32 bg-[rgba(21,74,122,0.3)]"></span>
        </figure>
    </section>

    <!-- What it actually does: just enough to believe -->
    <section
        class="grid gap-5 border-t border-t-[rgba(120,113,108,0.14)] pt-6"
    >
        <div class="grid max-w-[44rem] gap-2.5">
            <p class="eyebrow">What you get</p>
            <h2
                class="m-0 font-[Cormorant_Garamond,serif] text-[clamp(1.9rem,3vw,2.55rem)] leading-[0.98] text-[#2b241d]"
            >
                A system, not a feature.
            </h2>
            <p class="m-0 text-[#5b4f43] leading-relaxed max-w-[46rem]">
                GalexC is not one capability. It is the wiring between many
                capabilities -- designed so that they compound for you over
                time.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 xl:grid-cols-3">
            {
                capabilities.map((item) => (
                    <article class="grid gap-2 rounded-[1.2rem] border border-[rgba(120,113,108,0.14)] bg-[rgba(255,252,247,0.44)] p-5">
                        <h3 class="m-0 font-[IBM_Plex_Mono,monospace] text-[0.68rem] tracking-[0.18em] text-[#7a6d60] uppercase">
                            {item.label}
                        </h3>
                        <p class="m-0 text-[#4f4438] leading-relaxed">
                            {item.what}
                        </p>
                    </article>
                ))
            }
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- The seed: how you get it -->
    <section
        class="grid gap-5 border-t border-t-[rgba(120,113,108,0.14)] pt-6 max-w-[46rem]"
    >
        <div class="grid gap-2.5">
            <p class="eyebrow">The seed</p>
            <h2
                class="m-0 font-[Cormorant_Garamond,serif] text-[clamp(1.9rem,3vw,2.55rem)] leading-[0.98] text-[#2b241d]"
            >
                You do not sign up. You fork it.
            </h2>
        </div>
        <div class="grid gap-4 text-lg leading-[1.8] text-[#4f4438]">
            <p class="m-0">
                GalexC ships as a seed -- an opinionated, working system that
                you take ownership of from day one. It is not a SaaS you
                subscribe to. It is not a platform that holds your data. You
                fork it, you run it on your infrastructure, and you shape it
                around your work.
            </p>
            <p class="m-0">
                The seed is opinionated because it was built by someone doing
                real work with it every day. But the opinions are a starting
                point, not a constraint. Swap the database. Change the
                scheduling model. Rebuild services in your language of choice.
                Prefer a different agent harness? Use it -- GalexC is the
                system around the harness, not the harness itself. The
                architecture is designed for deliberate divergence -- you start
                from something that works and make it yours.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- The posture: keep Gilman's split -->
    <section class="border-t border-t-[rgba(120,113,108,0.14)] pt-6">
        <div
            class="grid grid-cols-1 overflow-hidden rounded-[1.35rem_0.95rem_1.15rem_0.92rem] border border-stone-400/14 bg-[linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(255,255,255,0.46),rgba(251,247,241,0.42))] shadow-[0_10px_28px_rgba(43,36,29,0.04),inset_0_1px_0_rgba(255,255,255,0.6)] sm:grid-cols-2"
        >
            <div
                class="grid gap-2 p-6 sm:border-r sm:border-stone-400/14 md:p-8"
            >
                <span
                    class="font-['IBM_Plex_Mono',monospace] text-[0.6rem] tracking-[0.22em] text-[#7a6d60] uppercase"
                >
                    01 / Posture
                </span>
                <p
                    class="m-0 text-[clamp(1.6rem,3.2vw,2.4rem)] leading-none whitespace-nowrap text-[#2b241d]"
                    style="font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', serif;"
                >
                    Personal first.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div
                class="grid gap-2 border-t border-stone-400/14 p-6 sm:border-t-0 md:p-8"
            >
                <span
                    class="font-['IBM_Plex_Mono',monospace] text-[0.6rem] tracking-[0.22em] text-[#154a7a] uppercase"
                >
                    02 / Standard
                </span>
                <p
                    class="m-0 text-[clamp(1.6rem,3.2vw,2.4rem)] leading-none whitespace-nowrap text-[#2b241d]"
                    style="font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', serif;"
                >
                    Professional grade.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Network tease -->
    <section
        class="grid gap-5 border-t border-t-[rgba(120,113,108,0.14)] pt-6 max-w-[46rem]"
    >
        <div class="grid gap-2.5">
            <p class="eyebrow">What comes next</p>
            <h2
                class="m-0 font-[Cormorant_Garamond,serif] text-[clamp(1.9rem,3vw,2.55rem)] leading-[0.98] text-[#2b241d]"
            >
                Your node connects.
            </h2>
        </div>
        <p class="m-0 text-lg leading-[1.8] text-[#4f4438]">
            GalexC starts as your personal AI. But it does not have to stay
            solo. When you are ready, your node connects to other nodes --
            your team, your org, your collaborators -- through a secure
            channel that keeps what is personal personal and what is shared
            shared. Your AI becomes part of something larger without losing
            what makes it yours.
        </p>
    </section>

    <!-- The gate -->
    <section
        class="grid gap-5 border-t border-t-[rgba(120,113,108,0.14)] pt-6 max-w-[46rem]"
    >
        <div class="grid gap-2.5">
            <p class="eyebrow">Access</p>
            <h2
                class="m-0 font-[Cormorant_Garamond,serif] text-[clamp(1.9rem,3vw,2.55rem)] leading-[0.98] text-[#2b241d]"
            >
                Invite only.
            </h2>
        </div>
        <div class="grid gap-4 text-lg leading-[1.8] text-[#4f4438]">
            <p class="m-0">
                GalexC is not generally available. It is currently offered on
                an individual, case-by-case basis to technical professionals
                who are serious about owning their AI infrastructure. If this
                resonates with the way you think about your work, request
                access.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-2">
            <a
                class="inline-block rounded-2xl border border-[rgba(21,74,122,0.22)] bg-[rgba(21,74,122,0.06)] px-6 py-3 font-[IBM_Plex_Mono,monospace] text-[0.72rem] tracking-[0.16em] text-[#154a7a] uppercase no-underline transition-[background,border-color,transform] duration-200 ease-out hover:-translate-y-px hover:border-[rgba(21,74,122,0.35)] hover:bg-[rgba(21,74,122,0.1)]"
                href="/?waitlist=open"
            >
                Request access
            </a>
        </div>
    </section>
</div>
